Need Spring to know which constructor. Options:
1. Add `@Autowired` to the 2-arg public constructor.
2. Better: make the 3-arg constructor `private` — Spring with multiple constructors still fails? Spring only auto-detects a single constructor. With multiple constructors, it needs `@Autowired` on one. Making it private, Spring may skip non-public constructors and use the sole public one. Actually Spring's `AutowiredAnnotationBeanPostProcessor` determines candidate constructors: if exactly one constructor and not `@Autowired`, uses it. If multiple, it looks for `@Autowired` annotated ones. Non-public constructors aren't considered candidates in `determineCandidateConstructors` unless annotated. Actually there is spring code: `determineCandidateConstructors` returns null if no annotated constructors; then `instantiateBean` uses default constructor (no args) -> fails. Hmm, but if there's exactly one constructor... The check is in `AutowiredAnnotationBeanPostProcessor.determineCandidateConstructors`: 
